<head>
<no>1</no><heading guid="_4eaebc12-8db3-4333-86d7-1bf0ba50fd17"
id="sec.1-he"><b>Name of Act</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This Act may be cited as the <legref
refid="act-1963-021" jurisd="NSW" type="act" check="unknown"><name
emphasis="yes"><i>Recovery of Imposts Act
1963</i></name></legref>.</txt></block>

<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 1:</b> Am 1993 No 96,
Sch 1 (2).</txt></content>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.1A">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_6ae72689-2d64-4cf5-907a-91256ff6225b"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.1A"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>1A</no><heading guid="_8823e676-2f48-482f-9b9d-edf01cc24013"
id="sec.1A-he"><b>Definitions</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">In this Act:</txt>
<deflist>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_ce368262-7543-4ad9-9ce2-c0ec6fe1e883"
id="def.invalidity"><b><i>invalidity</i></b></defterm> of taxation legislation
includes invalidity of a portion of the legislation or of an application of
the legislation.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_6e25e4c8-2929-4095-bc21-7a684163a13a"
id="def.pay"><b><i>pay</i></b></defterm> a tax includes recover the tax by
legal proceedings.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_cee458ed-91fd-465a-b7aa-0a8d53629152"
id="def.proceedings"><b><i>proceedings</i></b></defterm> includes proceedings
for an order in the nature of prohibition, certiorari or mandamus or for a
declaration or injunction or for any other relief.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_ea061c16-535b-4234-b6b3-013fa2887cd0"
id="def.tax"><b><i>tax</i></b></defterm> includes a fee, charge or other
impost.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_b2a6ae2a-5774-42d2-9b45-9423d4313cad"
id="def.taxationlegislation"><b><i>taxation legislation</i></b></defterm>
means:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_33d4b760-07f8-4b17-aa30-e5920558da1f" id="sec.1A-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">an Act imposing or relating to a tax,
or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_bf2a2acd-bfb7-4b5d-973e-248a9f58736a" id="sec.1A-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">a provision of such an Act,
or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_2adbd7b1-ed2e-4228-b236-1c58294d6bb0" id="sec.1A-para1.c">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">a regulation under such an Act,
or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_eb97ab79-940b-4a47-a850-2e4a50b72524" id="sec.1A-para1.d">
<no>(d)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">a provision of such a
regulation.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></deflist>
</block>

<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 1A:</b> Ins 1993 No 96,
Sch 1 (3).</txt></content>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_ef287cfa-7c5f-411f-93ac-8eda8003dc49"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>2</no><heading guid="_3bc7f987-cf0d-4a30-9645-ee6c775f38d6"
id="sec.2-he"><b>Limitation on time for the bringing of proceedings to recover
taxes</b></heading></head>

<pre type="auto-inserted">

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.2-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_57f94c9b-5975-4f2e-abe3-7f4a7d0c9b0d"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.2-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">No proceedings shall be brought to recover from
the Crown or the Government or the State of New South Wales or any Minister of
the Crown, or from any corporation, officer or person or out of any fund to
whom or which it was paid, the amount or any part of the amount paid by way of
tax or purported tax and recoverable on restitutionary grounds (including but
not limited to mistake of law or fact):</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_903ee76c-1eca-4b6e-8ad9-f8f3b93900d4" id="sec.2-ssec.1-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">in the case of a payment made before the
commencement of this Act, after the expiration of the time within which such
proceedings but for the enactment of this Act might have been brought or the
expiration of twelve months after the date of the commencement of this Act,
whichever period first expires, or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_c044f855-3c42-494d-bc04-bbd8035c2c16" id="sec.2-ssec.1-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">in the case of a payment made subsequent to the
commencement of this Act, after the expiration of twelve months after the date
of payment.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>
</pre>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.2-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_478f43db-7ed9-4186-804e-1cfe1c399d88"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.2-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Subsection (1) does not apply to any proceedings
brought pursuant to any specific provisions of any Act:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_90cbaecf-23a1-49a7-a0df-ed1d7ba46909" id="sec.2-ssec.2-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">providing for the mode of challenging the
validity or for the recovery of the whole or any part of any tax actually
paid, and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_fd726486-bf25-4fa1-9d26-3a6cc3225779" id="sec.2-ssec.2-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">specifying a different period within which such
proceedings must be brought.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.2-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_4e7af75b-3cd6-48be-9b6c-0f00a4ed6efa"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.2-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Without affecting the generality of this section,
and for the avoidance of doubt, it is declared that this section applies to
proceedings for the recovery of money (paid by way of tax or purported tax) on
the ground of, or on grounds that include, the invalidity of taxation
legislation.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.2-ssec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_650ab253-f7f2-4d35-9ef0-d26f39d3a841"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.2-ssec.4"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(4)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This section does not apply to money that is not
recoverable because of section 3.</txt></block></tier>


<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 2:</b> Am 1993 No 96,
Sch 1 (4); 1995 No 98, Sch 6 (1)&#8211;(4).</txt></content>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_f2d71dfd-9e2d-487b-9bf7-dd068ce5a5da"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>3</no><heading guid="_3f148440-8068-4750-b284-01b7c1a58e7e"
id="sec.3-he"><b>Certain taxes not recoverable following non-legislative
changes of the law</b></heading></head>

<pre type="auto-inserted">

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.3-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_bbcdafa7-c1b9-40f6-943b-fbada550c9ca"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">In this section, <defterm type="definition"
guid="_b32a2d0a-cb9b-4fe6-9aa2-97a62b324dd4"
id="sec.3-def.nonlegislativechangeofthelaw"><b><i>non-legislative change of
the law</i></b></defterm> means a change of the law or of legal principles, or
a change in what is generally perceived to be the state of the law or of legal
principles, but does not include a change made by
legislation.</txt></block></tier>
</pre>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.3-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_4b3e94b1-c9a2-4b75-a913-22a5178d1ba8"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Money paid by way of tax or purported tax is not
recoverable on any of the grounds referred to in subsection (3), if:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_ca3b0123-2d00-46d4-8320-361610812f82" id="sec.3-ssec.2-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the ground came into existence because of a
non-legislative change of the law, and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_d9e855b0-164e-4569-b534-249fd8f01c00" id="sec.3-ssec.2-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the money was paid before the
change.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.3-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_d228f9f0-e5a1-40b8-b56f-381e3db8935a"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The grounds are:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_0e02bc36-9b65-4c70-ada3-14e627916b09" id="sec.3-ssec.3-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the ground of invalidity of any taxation
legislation, or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_c62a03cf-c8a8-409a-954b-d95cad8ab4ef" id="sec.3-ssec.3-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the ground of mistake (whether of law or of fact)
as to the validity or invalidity of any taxation legislation,
or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_091e3e8f-ec80-4065-9eb0-c8fa109d01f8" id="sec.3-ssec.3-para1.c">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">any other restitutionary ground relating to the
validity or invalidity of any taxation legislation.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.3-ssec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_7a6a5bb7-f0e0-4802-966a-1b75b07d5d8c"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3-ssec.4"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(4)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Subsection (2) does not apply to proceedings for
the recovery of money that, assuming the legislation concerned had been valid,
would have represented an overpayment of a tax, if the legislation provides
for the refund of the money.</txt></block></tier>


<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>ss 3&#8211;6:</b> Ins
1993 No 96, Sch 1 (5).</txt></content>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_118e6635-42a2-4837-97cf-7fa0f3f8a12e"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>4</no><heading guid="_40c6e10c-bb80-4711-9bf7-cf9b4083ed64"
id="sec.4-he"><b>Passing on of tax</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.4-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_6d6921a3-4d0e-4c45-9a53-5b0e2ee0f1d0"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Proceedings referred to in section 2 or 3 (4) to
recover an amount paid are however maintainable only to the extent that the
person bringing the proceedings (<defterm type="definition"
guid="_8c411986-9c6f-4727-ab0c-3f81c234cf65"
id="sec.4-def.theclaimant"><b><i>the claimant</i></b></defterm>) satisfies the
court that the claimant has not charged to or recovered from, and will not
charge to or recover from, any other person any amount in respect of the whole
or any part of the amount paid. This applies whether or not any such amount
has been itemised or otherwise separately identified in any invoice or other
documentation.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.4-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_d669ce9e-7a18-4104-929c-0426449d8ecd"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">A reference in this section to the claimant
extends to a predecessor, successor or assignee of the
claimant.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.4-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_b08ecb4c-0048-4027-853e-7cbab0642e88"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This section has effect despite anything in
section 2 or 3, or in any other Act.</txt></block></tier>


<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>ss 3&#8211;6:</b> Ins
1993 No 96, Sch 1 (5).</txt></content>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.5">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_f287fbdb-9009-4a09-8560-7230d3a57c51"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>5</no><heading guid="_77bee0d6-1799-4206-87fa-8c2b5abd2373"
id="sec.5-he"><b>Ending of right of recovery</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">If because of this Act money paid by way of tax
or purported tax ceases to be or is not recoverable, the right to recover the
money is extinguished.</txt></block>

<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>ss 3&#8211;6:</b> Ins
1993 No 96, Sch 1 (5).</txt></content>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.6">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_e5d199c4-d0a0-48d3-a304-b39fac20656b"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>6</no><heading guid="_b3bcd703-c73e-4dfe-9774-7f454b98d4ce"
id="sec.6-he"><b>Characterisation of this Act</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The provisions of this Act are to be regarded as
part of the substantive law of the State.</txt></block>

<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>ss 3&#8211;6:</b> Ins
1993 No 96, Sch 1 (5).</txt></content>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.7">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_b4e4a722-964d-403d-9316-36fb861733be"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>7</no><heading guid="_cbf7f002-0ce9-4833-995c-2eea73a9b622"
id="sec.7-he"><b>Application</b></heading></head>

<pre type="auto-inserted">

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_9a666c5f-a806-4c6b-81a3-7f24c8885598"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This Act applies to money paid whether
voluntarily or under compulsion, and applies whether or not the payment was
made under protest, and applies whether or not the payment was made under the
authority or purported authority of any Act.</txt></block></tier>
</pre>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_d96897df-5a20-42a0-a74c-767659b51dde"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This Act has effect despite the provisions of any
other Act.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_e62a8f7b-8506-4710-86bd-5a8f66274867"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The amendments made to this Act by the <legref
jurisd="NSW" type="act" check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Limitation of
Actions (Recovery of Imposts) Amendment Act 1993</i></name></legref> apply to
money paid, and proceedings commenced, whether before or after the
commencement of that Act.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_80223e44-b74c-4be5-9a71-fa19f35b5baa"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.4"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(4)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Sections 1A and 2 (1)&#8211;(3) of this Act as
amended by the <legref jurisd="NSW" type="act" check="unknown"><name
emphasis="yes"><i>Limitation of Actions (Recovery of Imposts) Amendment Act
1993</i></name></legref> have effect for all purposes, and are taken always to
have had effect for all purposes, as from the commencement of this
Act.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.5">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_e0fa6a4c-5c74-4f46-bd57-3b641ee38045"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.5"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(5)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The amendments made to this Act by Schedule 6 to
the <legref jurisd="NSW" type="act" check="unknown"><name
emphasis="yes"><i>State Revenue Legislation Further Amendment Act
1995</i></name></legref>:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_fc58a0e9-4584-421b-b0fb-919bb7c96002" id="sec.7-ssec.5-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">apply to money paid, and proceedings commenced,
whether before or after the commencement of the amendments,
and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_da311c41-7391-4daa-b012-37dceaa40dc8" id="sec.7-ssec.5-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">have effect for all purposes, and are taken
always to have effect for all purposes, as from the commencement of this
Act.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>


<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 7:</b> Ins 1993 No 96,
Sch 1 (5). Am 1995 No 98, Sch 6 (5) (6).</txt></content>
</level>
</content>


